  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of integrated lifesaving WASH services to drought affected population in Afgoye district of Lower Shabelle region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspan style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif color: black&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;gtNew Ways is proposing 8-month integrated WASH
project targeting the most drought affected populations in Afgoye&#xA0;district
reaching a total of 10,000 persons including (2,750 men, 5,000 women, 1,250 girls,
and 1,000 boys). In this project, New Ways is aimed to improve access to
life-saving WASH services for Afgoye&#xA0;IDPs, Vulnerable host communities with
recognition of people of disabilities, and the most vulnerable population
through: -ltbrgt
1) Provision of safe water drinking with water trucking for 50 days period.
benefiting 3,600 i.e 900 men, 2000 women, 400 girls, and 300 boys) drought
affected IDPs and host communities will be under taken.ltbrgt
2) New Ways Organization will also construct 80 normal latrines to benefit
residents in Afgoye&#xA0;IDP sites which will also receive the clean water and
hygiene promotions and hygiene kits, 12 additional latrines will be preserved
for people living with disabilities who are living in the target locations.ltbrgt
3) 1200&#xA0;Households will benefit from hygiene kit distribution and hygiene
awareness.&#xA0;ltbrgt
4) 10 Hygiene promoters will be recruited and trained&#xA0;lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspan style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif color: black&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;gt5) Hygiene promotion
campaign will be undertakenltbrgt
6) Monitoring and supervision will be conducted twice&#xA0;during the project periodltbrgt
7) Rehabilitation of 4 shallow wells and 1 boreholeltbrgt
8) 5 WASH committees will be established and trained to improve all preventive
measures against the risks of AWD/cholera outbreaks in Afgoye&#xA0;districtltbrgt
9) Chlorination of the wells through recruited hygiene promoters i.e 6 shallow
wells per week for the project periodltbrgt
10) 63&#xA0;sanitation tools will be procured and distributed.ltbrgtltbrgtlt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
